  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Movement Governance and Strategic Partnerships</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This budget area covers the Movement Governance work of the International Directorate and Strategic Partnerships carried out by the Humanitarian Policy Department. These two areas can be separate in nature but are also often overlapping which is the reason that they are combined under one specific project. The Movement Governance aspect of this work relates to the formal role we play within the Movement relating to Statutory areas of work. This includes the British Red Cross role on the Governing Board of the IFRC and our contribution to statutory meetings including the General Assembly (every two years) the Council of Delegates (every two years) and the International Conference (every four years). The Strategic Partnerships side of this work is in relation to initiatives that we carry out with our Movement Partners in particular sister National Societies and also the IFRC and the ICRC. Specific partnerships on areas of humanitarian policy and substance will help us to achieve the pillars highlighted above in the Strategic Alignment section.</narrative>
  </description>
